{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340936",
      "title": "Making Sense Of The Full Route Cache",
      "lectureOrder": 187,
      "videoOrder": 173,
      "sourceHash": "4904608672f75679e2a7e10038d344e00d17968eaf47228c7653bd87cfb80280",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.84,
          "end": 2.16,
          "en": "So we did now learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 4.71,
          "en": "about a lot of different cache settings,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.71,
          "end": 7.8,
          "en": "and we learned how those settings can be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.8,
          "end": 9.87,
          "en": "to control the data cache.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.87,
          "end": 12.15,
          "en": "Now, besides that data cache,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.15,
          "end": 15.36,
          "en": "NextJS also has a full route cache,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.36,
          "end": 18.33,
          "en": "and that's actually the kind of cache",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.33,
          "end": 22.293,
          "en": "we saw in action in this application before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.22,
          "end": 26.809,
          "en": "Because that full route cache is actually already created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.809,
          "end": 29.703,
          "en": "and initialized at build time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.66,
          "end": 34.29,
          "en": "which simply means that if I stop that development server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.29,
          "end": 38.07,
          "en": "and I build this NextJS application for production",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.07,
          "end": 41.88,
          "en": "by running npm run build, NextJS goes ahead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.88,
          "end": 45.57,
          "en": "and pre-renders all the pages of this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.57,
          "end": 49.35,
          "en": "unless they're dynamic pages with a dynamic parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.35,
          "end": 50.88,
          "en": "because there, by default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.88,
          "end": 55.88,
          "en": "it doesn't know all the possible dynamic parameter values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.16,
          "end": 60.6,
          "en": "but it pre-renders all the pages it's able to pre-render.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.6,
          "end": 64.32,
          "en": "You also see that here, that all those pages marked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.32,
          "end": 66.72,
          "en": "with a dot were pre-rendered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.72,
          "end": 68.85,
          "en": "so the messages page, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.85,
          "end": 72.09,
          "en": "was pre-rendered, as you can tell,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.09,
          "end": 74.28,
          "en": "and the implication of that is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.28,
          "end": 78.06,
          "en": "that when we start the production server with npm start,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.06,
          "end": 80.531,
          "en": "it will actually be those pre-rendered pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.531,
          "end": 84.03,
          "en": "that we see out of the box, and those pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.03,
          "end": 88.05,
          "en": "are actually cached by NextJS, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.05,
          "end": 92.34,
          "en": "Therefore, now with that production server up and running,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.34,
          "end": 96.03,
          "en": "if I clear and restart my backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.03,
          "end": 99.63,
          "en": "we will actually see no log message at all here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.63,
          "end": 102.72,
          "en": "when I reload that messages page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.72,
          "end": 105.45,
          "en": "and we see no log message here at all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.45,
          "end": 109.65,
          "en": "because that page was pre-rendered at build time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.65,
          "end": 111.78,
          "en": "and it's cached, and it's now always",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.78,
          "end": 115.56,
          "en": "that pre-rendered cached page that's being served here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.56,
          "end": 119.07,
          "en": "no matter how often I reload or navigate away and come back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.07,
          "end": 122.04,
          "en": "It's always that pre-rendered page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.04,
          "end": 125.37,
          "en": "Hence, we got no logs here on that backend server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.37,
          "end": 126.99,
          "en": "Now, that's, of course, fine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.99,
          "end": 129.69,
          "en": "as long as the data here doesn't change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.69,
          "end": 132.93,
          "en": "and in this dummy application with that dummy backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.93,
          "end": 135.06,
          "en": "that's the case because the data served",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 135.06,
          "end": 137.88,
          "en": "from that dummy backend does never change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.88,
          "end": 140.334,
          "en": "but we saw before in the previous section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.334,
          "end": 144.3,
          "en": "where we learned about data mutations with NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.3,
          "end": 148.56,
          "en": "that this can be a problem if we have data that does change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 148.56,
          "end": 152.1,
          "en": "because due to that pre-rendered cached page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.1,
          "end": 156.99,
          "en": "NextJS never re-renders and updates that page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 156.99,
          "end": 160.82999999999998,
          "en": "And that's another thing that will be controlled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 160.82999999999998,
          "end": 164.57999999999998,
          "en": "by setting one of these cache settings here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 164.57999999999998,
          "end": 168.39,
          "en": "For example, if I set force dynamic to this entire file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 168.39,
          "end": 171.57,
          "en": "to make sure that there is no data caching,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 171.57,
          "end": 175.65,
          "en": "I automatically also disable the full route cache",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 175.65,
          "end": 178.53,
          "en": "for this page, and I make sure that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 178.53,
          "end": 181.41,
          "en": "instead of pre-rendering and caching this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 181.41,
          "end": 184.26,
          "en": "NextJS will always re-render that page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.26,
          "end": 186.393,
          "en": "whenever a request is sent to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 187.26,
          "end": 191.073,
          "en": "which ensures that we're always fetching fresh data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 192.12,
          "end": 195.87,
          "en": "and that's why, when I enable this dynamic constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 195.87,
          "end": 200.52,
          "en": "and set it to force dynamic here, and I then save that file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 200.52,
          "end": 205.52,
          "en": "and I then rebuild my project to rebuild it for production,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 208.02,
          "end": 211.92000000000002,
          "en": "now, this messages route has a different symbol here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 211.92000000000002,
          "end": 214.47,
          "en": "which means that it's a dynamic page now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 214.47,
          "end": 217.32,
          "en": "which is server-rendered on demand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 217.32,
          "end": 219.78300000000002,
          "en": "as you can tell down here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 221.79,
          "end": 223.95,
          "en": "And indeed, that's what we can see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 223.95,
          "end": 227.37,
          "en": "when we start the production server with npm start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 227.37,
          "end": 229.86,
          "en": "Now, if we take a look at this backend log,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 229.86,
          "end": 232.41,
          "en": "if I reload this page a couple of times,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 232.41,
          "end": 234.81,
          "en": "I see a bunch of logs here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 234.81,
          "end": 238.07999999999998,
          "en": "because now it's not just the data cache that's cleared,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 238.07999999999998,
          "end": 239.724,
          "en": "but also that full route cache,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 239.724,
          "end": 243.175,
          "en": "and we make sure that it's not some pre-rendered page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 243.175,
          "end": 245.913,
          "en": "that's reused over and over again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 247.23,
          "end": 249.424,
          "en": "Of course, we don't have to use this setting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 249.424,
          "end": 252.36,
          "en": "to make sure that we see updated data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 252.36,
          "end": 255.456,
          "en": "A different approach would be to revalidate the cache",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 255.456,
          "end": 258.27,
          "en": "of a specific page on demand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 258.27,
          "end": 261.75,
          "en": "with the revalidate path function we already used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 261.75,
          "end": 265.17,
          "en": "in the previous section, and that's now a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 265.17,
          "end": 267.33,
          "en": "which we'll revisit in the next lecture",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 267.33,
          "end": 269.55,
          "en": "before we then thereafter will take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 269.55,
          "end": 270.884,
          "en": "at how we can manage caching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 270.884,
          "end": 274.74,
          "en": "if we're not sending a request to a separate backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 274.74,
          "end": 276.96,
          "en": "but instead to some other data source,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 276.96,
          "end": 280.713,
          "en": "like a database we manage in the NextJS application.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
